#[BOOK TEXT] This should take place during the book dream. There is history
#but there must be also the hints that the book and the player are one and
#the same, made of the very same thing.
#
#By then the thought had already
#entered my mind.
#The decision was hasty, we 
#thought we needed more time...
#...and more time we got.
#All the time in the world.
#
#Can you imagine now, that the
#solution became clear to me the
#very moment after the seals
#closed?
#
# Game intro, the player appears.

[[game-intro-001]]{{
I must have travelled here from
afar, consumed by obsession
guided by a will not of my own.
}}

[[game-intro-002]]{{
My life before this moment is all
confused recollections, shards,
a mere memory of a dream.
}}

[[game-intro-003]]{{
How long have I been dreaming
all of these drifting fragments?
Did I simply remember them?
}}

[[game-intro-004]]{{
These pictures, too clear in the
mind to be just imaginations, too
far to be my own rememberances.
}}

[[game-intro-005]]{{
Proud ships charging the storm.
The bravest of people, most alive
around the rage and the fury.
}}

[[game-intro-006]]{{
Wise and dutiful guardians,
benevolent, alert, confident.
Always alone at their watchtowers.
}}

[[game-intro-007]]{{
Eyes watching in the jungle,
keepers of ancient rituals,
a tradition of secrecy.
}}

[[game-intro-008]]{{
Four souls, a long journey that
ends a cycle, or perhaps keeps
the cycle from breaking...
}}

#[land imaginery, some sort of canyon?]
[[game-intro-009]]{{
Pilgrims to a land glimpsed
through half-closed eyes,
secret, bent, intersecting.
}}

[[game-intro-010]]{{
At night I kept marching, onwards
always. Closer and closer,
maybe even as I slept.
}}

[[game-intro-011]]{{
I marched, and tried to remember.
Or I dreamt, and I created.
Is it not all the same?
}}

#[Tower walls, scrolling up!]
[[game-intro-012]]{{
But then, I raised my head and
there I could see the tower.
Ever nearer. Was I there yet?
}}

[[game-intro-013]]{{
It is like stone needle to the
ground, a sole constant, a pulse,
a lighthouse, a call. Always.
[@np]
Calling.
[@np]
Calling.
[@np]
Calling me.
}}

[[game-intro-014]]{{
But none of that, of my memories
and my thoughts, of these dreams
and reveries matters now.
[@np]
I must have travelled here from
afar, but I am finally here,
where I belong.
[@np]
Now, that I can almost touch it
I can no longer hear the call.
[@np]
But there has to be a reason.
}}

